US-047 is not complete. I did not emit the COMPLETE signal, and I made no source changes this pass.

**Status: Partial.**

- **Done (CPU runtime, `engine/world`):** tiles, LOD by distance, stitching by vertex morph, normals, four-layer splat weights, and height query. Fourteen fixture cases in `tests/src/world_terrain_tests.cpp` cover coverage, holes, LOD switching, and normals. The earlier entry records the Linux and Windows CPU gates and the ASan/UBSan run as passing.
- **Not done:** the renderer side of the story. There is no terrain draw path in `SceneRenderer`, no splat shading, no shadow or depth participation, and no RT geometry. `rt_effects_geometry_support` still reports heightfield terrain as unsupported. There is also no GPU terrain fixture and no `engine_bench` terrain workload.
- **Gates:** I did not re-run them this pass because no source changed since the last entry. The Windows GPU suites and the acceptance bench have nothing terrain-specific to test yet, so they have not been run.

**Why I stopped here:** the renderer change touches the indexed, indirect, meshlet, shadow, and RT paths of `scene_renderer.cpp` (about 3,800 lines). Verifying it needs a Windows GPU run, and I would not leave a partial edit to that file unverified.

**Recommended next pass:** use vertex colour for the four splat weights, since the CPU mesh already carries normalised weights per vertex. Add a terrain draw that uploads each `TerrainTileMesh`, then wire it into shadows and RT, then add the GPU fixture and bench workload. Then run the Windows gate batch.

